<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Union Defence Force (South Africa)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1912">1912</a>–<a href="/years/1957">1957</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Union Defence Force was the military of the Union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, established by the Defence Act of 1912. It fought in both world wars, conquering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-south-west-africa">German South West Africa</a> in 1915 and serving in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a>, on the Western Front, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and it was renamed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-african-defence-force">South African Defence Force</a> in 1957.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/union-defence-force-south-africa.jpg" alt="Union Defence Force (South Africa)" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vectorebus · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Union_Defence_Force_emblem.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
